<b>But the timing and scale were not equal.</b>

240
01:07:48,766 --> 01:07:50,133
<b>Timothy Snyder, working</b>

241
01:07:50,133 --> 01:07:51,466
<b>from Moptikka's research,</b>

242
01:07:51,566 --> 01:07:54,166
<b>puts the wider conflict at roughly 70,000</b>

243
01:07:54,199 --> 01:07:57,133
<b>dead Poles to 20,000 dead Ukrainians.</b>

244
01:07:57,266 --> 01:07:59,099
<b>And it wasn't Poles against Ukrainians as</b>

245
01:07:59,099 --> 01:08:00,466
<b>whole peoples either.</b>

246
01:08:00,833 --> 01:08:03,400
<b>The UPA's own security service shot</b>

247
01:08:03,400 --> 01:08:05,599
<b>Ukrainians at considered unreliable,</b>

248
01:08:05,933 --> 01:08:08,500
<b>including men who refused to kill Poles.</b>

249
01:08:08,666 --> 01:08:09,566
<b>So the part about</b>

250
01:08:09,599 --> 01:08:11,266
<b>Polish reprisals is real.</b>

251
01:08:11,766 --> 01:08:14,066
<b>But most serious historians don't accept</b>

252
01:08:14,066 --> 01:08:15,333
<b>the spontaneous part.</b>

253
01:08:15,500 --> 01:08:16,866
<b>Jared McBride calls</b>

254
01:08:16,866 --> 01:08:18,066
<b>this ethnic cleansing.</b>

255
01:08:18,266 --> 01:08:19,433
<b>Ivan Katamzowski</b>

256
01:08:19,433 --> 01:08:21,300
<b>rejects the genocide label,</b>

257
01:08:21,433 --> 01:08:23,566
<b>but still calls it one-sided ethnic</b>

258
01:08:23,566 --> 01:08:27,233
<b>cleansing organized by the OUNB, the UPA,</b>

259
01:08:27,333 --> 01:08:28,800
<b>and its security service.</b>

260
01:08:29,233 --> 01:08:31,133
<b>Moptikka goes further and calls it</b>

261
01:08:31,133 --> 01:08:32,766
<b>genocidal ethnic cleansing.</b>

262
01:08:33,166 --> 01:08:35,000
<b>The disagreement between those historians</b>

263
01:08:35,000 --> 01:08:36,833
<b>is narrower than the political one.</b>

264
01:08:36,966 --> 01:08:39,266
<b>They agree this was organized violence to</b>

265
01:08:39,266 --> 01:08:41,366
<b>remove the Polish population from Wolnia.</b>

266
01:08:41,866 --> 01:08:44,266
<b>They disagree about whether the aim was</b>

267
01:08:44,266 --> 01:08:46,000
<b>removal or destruction,</b>

268
01:08:46,333 --> 01:08:48,100
<b>and about how close the surviving</b>

269
01:08:48,100 --> 01:08:50,533
<b>documents take us to the men at the top.</b>

270
01:08:50,699 --> 01:08:52,800
<b>The report I started the video with is an</b>

271
01:08:52,800 --> 01:08:54,600
<b>example of what we do have.</b>

272
01:08:55,166 --> 01:08:56,199
<b>A commander had just</b>

273
01:08:56,199 --> 01:08:58,133
<b>destroyed two Polish villages,</b>

274
01:08:58,233 --> 01:08:59,433
<b>and he was reporting a</b>

275
01:08:59,433 --> 01:09:01,833
<b>Finnish job up to his superiors.</b>

276
01:09:02,266 --> 01:09:04,133
<b>That is not a mob of angry people.</b>

277
01:09:04,266 --> 01:09:05,899
<b>It is an officer working</b>

278
01:09:05,899 --> 01:09:07,399
<b>inside a chain of command.</b>

279
01:09:07,766 --> 01:09:10,133
<b>And if we look at UPA internal directives</b>

280
01:09:10,133 --> 01:09:12,466
<b>from 1944, one ends</b>

281
01:09:12,466 --> 01:09:13,699
<b>with a standing greeting.</b>

282
01:09:14,266 --> 01:09:16,666
<b>Weapons ready, death to Poles.</b>

283
01:09:17,033 --> 01:09:18,533
<b>But if we follow these reports back to</b>

284
01:09:18,533 --> 01:09:19,800
<b>the top, at a certain</b>

285
01:09:19,800 --> 01:09:21,300
<b>point the paper stops.</b>

286
01:09:21,566 --> 01:09:24,166
<b>The Volian UPA commander was Dmytrio</b>

287
01:09:24,166 --> 01:09:26,899
<b>Krijakzkiewski, known as Klim Stavur.</b>

288
01:09:27,300 --> 01:09:29,066
<b>Administrative and military orders</b>

289
01:09:29,066 --> 01:09:30,966
<b>bearing his signatures survive.</b>

290
01:09:31,066 --> 01:09:33,500
<b>Some Polish historians cite the directive</b>

291
01:09:33,533 --> 01:09:34,633
<b>they describe as Klim</b>

292
01:09:34,633 --> 01:09:35,800
<b>Stavur's signed order</b>

293
01:09:35,800 --> 01:09:37,500
<b>to destroy the Polish population.</b>

294
01:09:37,666 --> 01:09:39,433
<b>But the original comes from the same</b>

295
01:09:39,500 --> 01:09:42,266
<b>archive complex nobody can inspect today.</b>

296
01:09:42,366 --> 01:09:44,166
<b>So the real problem is not that nobody</b>

297
01:09:44,166 --> 01:09:46,699
<b>has ever claimed a signed order existed.</b>

298
01:09:46,933 --> 01:09:48,666
<b>It's that nobody can produce an</b>

299
01:09:48,666 --> 01:09:49,966
<b>authenticated kill</b>

300
01:09:50,000 --> 01:09:51,600
<b>order bearing his signature</b>

301
01:09:51,766 --> 01:09:53,633
<b>that all sites can inspect.</b>

302
01:09:54,000 --> 01:09:55,333
<b>The closest evidence we do</b>

303
01:09:55,333 --> 01:09:57,000
<b>have are two pieces of paper,</b>

304
01:09:57,266 --> 01:09:58,166
<b>both from a UPA</b>

305
01:09:58,166 --> 01:10:00,333
<b>commander named Yuri Stelmakzuk.</b>

306
01:10:00,633 --> 01:10:02,933
<b>The first is a confession from 1945.</b>

307
01:10:03,699 --> 01:10:06,233
<b>After he was captured, Stelmakzuk told</b>

308
01:10:06,233 --> 01:10:08,399
<b>Soviet interrogators that Klyrzkiewski</b>

309
01:10:08,566 --> 01:10:10,933
<b>had given him the secret directive about</b>

310
01:10:10,933 --> 01:10:11,866
<b>the complete physical</b>

311
01:10:11,866 --> 01:10:13,800
<b>destruction of the Polish population.</b>

312
01:10:13,933 --> 01:10:15,766
<b>That confession was recorded under duress</b>

313
01:10:15,766 --> 01:10:17,333
<b>and in the interrogator's wording,</b>

314
01:10:17,533 --> 01:10:18,766
<b>so it cannot be treated</b>

315
01:10:18,966 --> 01:10:20,500
<b>like a voluntary statement.</b>

316
01:10:20,766 --> 01:10:23,066
<b>Viatrovich says Soviet investigators</b>

317
01:10:23,066 --> 01:10:25,466
<b>fabricated or manipulated it to discredit</b>

318
01:10:25,466 --> 01:10:27,300
<b>the Ukrainian independence movement.</b>

319
01:10:27,800 --> 01:10:30,433
<b>But a copy sits in Ukraine's own archive,</b>

320
01:10:30,733 --> 01:10:32,366
<b>filed there in 1963.</b>

321
01:10:32,966 --> 01:10:35,233
<b>Another published copy carries a Soviet</b>

322
01:10:35,233 --> 01:10:36,166
<b>general's handwritten</b>

323
01:10:36,166 --> 01:10:38,600
<b>notes, dated April 1945.</b>

324
01:10:39,133 --> 01:10:40,533
<b>That makes it difficult to say the</b>

325
01:10:40,566 --> 01:10:41,600
<b>document itself was</b>

326
01:10:41,600 --> 01:10:43,266
<b>invented decades later.</b>

327
01:10:43,433 --> 01:10:44,899
<b>It does not prove the confession was</b>

328
01:10:44,899 --> 01:10:46,466
<b>voluntary or that every</b>

329
01:10:46,466 --> 01:10:47,866
<b>word came from Stelmakzuk.</b>

330
01:10:48,266 --> 01:10:51,133
<b>The second piece is older and stronger, a</b>

331
01:10:51,133 --> 01:10:52,899
<b>letter from June 1943.</b>

332
01:10:53,333 --> 01:10:54,433
<b>Written while the killing</b>

333
01:10:54,433 --> 01:10:56,333
<b>was underway, Stelmakzuk</b>

334
01:10:56,633 --> 01:10:58,066
<b>doubted that the order had come from</b>

335
01:10:58,066 --> 01:11:00,766
<b>Klyrzkiewski, so he wrote to the OUN</b>

336
01:11:00,899 --> 01:11:02,033
<b>leadership to check.</b>

337
01:11:02,466 --> 01:11:04,399
<b>In that letter, he repeated the same</b>

338
01:11:04,399 --> 01:11:06,466
<b>secret directive and said it had been</b>

339
01:11:06,466 --> 01:11:07,833
<b>given by word of mouth.</b>

340
01:11:07,933 --> 01:11:09,533
<b>We do not know whether he received an</b>

341
01:11:09,600 --> 01:11:12,233
<b>answer, but he carried the order out.</b>

342
01:11:12,566 --> 01:11:14,766
<b>Stelmakzuk signed the letter, but the</b>

343
01:11:14,766 --> 01:11:16,600
<b>letter reports an oral order.</b>

344
01:11:16,899 --> 01:11:18,633
<b>It is not the order itself.</b>

345
01:11:18,933 --> 01:11:20,133
<b>And there's one more problem.</b>

346
01:11:20,566 --> 01:11:22,166
<b>Nobody has been able to inspect the</b>

347
01:11:22,166 --> 01:11:24,133
<b>original file the letter is cited from.</b>

348
01:11:24,399 --> 01:11:26,366
<b>It was restricted again, it was</b>

349
01:11:26,366 --> 01:11:28,300
<b>restricted again or lost around the</b>

350
01:11:28,333 --> 01:11:29,800
<b>collapse of the Soviet Union.</b>

351
01:11:30,199 --> 01:11:33,033
<b>So the public evidence is a transcription</b>

352
01:11:33,033 --> 01:11:34,699
<b>reproduced by historians.</b>

353
01:11:35,133 --> 01:11:36,600
<b>That is strong evidence</b>

354
01:11:36,600 --> 01:11:38,366
<b>of a reported oral order.</b>

355
01:11:38,766 --> 01:11:41,100
<b>It is not Klyrzkiewski's signature.</b>

356
01:11:41,766 --> 01:11:43,733
<b>So where does that leave us?</b>

357
01:11:43,899 --> 01:11:45,366
<b>The record shows an organized</b>

358
01:11:45,399 --> 01:11:47,066
<b>campaign under Klyrzkiewski.</b>

359
01:11:47,866 --> 01:11:49,833
<b>It does not show an authenticated order</b>

360
01:11:49,833 --> 01:11:51,800
<b>from him that would settle the argument</b>

361
01:11:51,800 --> 01:11:53,433
<b>about his exact intent.</b>

362
01:11:54,000 --> 01:11:55,899
<b>And that's why this argument survives.</b>

363
01:11:56,166 --> 01:11:58,466
<b>Ukraine has offered Poland some things.</b>

364
01:11:58,933 --> 01:12:00,300
<b>The two countries signed the</b>

365
01:12:00,300 --> 01:12:03,100
<b>reconciliation declaration in 1997.</b>

366
01:12:03,766 --> 01:12:06,300
<b>And in 2023, their presidents</b>

367
01:12:06,300 --> 01:12:07,833
<b>mourned the victims together.</b>

368
01:12:08,266 --> 01:12:10,166
<b>But Poland still wants to dig up the</b>

369
01:12:10,166 --> 01:12:11,833
<b>graves and name the dead.</b>

370
01:12:12,500 --> 01:12:13,366
<b>And the unresolved</b>

371
01:12:13,366 --> 01:12:15,500
<b>history hands Russia a weapon.</b>

372
01:12:16,000 --> 01:12:18,466
<b>Moscow takes this very real crime and</b>

373
01:12:18,466 --> 01:12:19,466
<b>uses it to claim that</b>

374
01:12:19,466 --> 01:12:21,766
<b>Ukraine itself is a Nazi state.</b>

375
01:12:22,300 --> 01:12:24,333
<b>But nothing in these documents proves</b>

376
01:12:24,333 --> 01:12:25,833
<b>that about modern Ukraine.</b>

377
01:12:26,766 --> 01:12:29,199
<b>Poland still arms and supports Ukraine</b>

378
01:12:29,266 --> 01:12:31,199
<b>because its own security depends on an</b>

379
01:12:31,233 --> 01:12:32,433
<b>independent Ukraine.</b>

380
01:12:33,166 --> 01:12:35,533
<b>So it condemns the UPA while helping</b>

381
01:12:35,533 --> 01:12:37,066
<b>modern Ukraine survive.</b>

382
01:12:37,333 --> 01:12:38,866
<b>This is not unique to Ukraine.</b>

383
01:12:39,000 --> 01:12:40,966
<b>In my own Belgium, we still have statues</b>

384
01:12:40,966 --> 01:12:42,000
<b>and squares honoring</b>

385
01:12:42,000 --> 01:12:45,266
<b>Leopold II after everything</b>

386
01:12:45,966 --> 01:12:47,600
<b>There's nothing wrong with looking to the</b>

387
01:12:47,633 --> 01:12:48,833
<b>past for heroes when</b>

388
01:12:48,833 --> 01:12:50,033
<b>you're in a fight now.</b>

389
01:12:50,466 --> 01:12:53,199
<b>What is wrong is burying what they did.</b>

390
01:12:53,433 --> 01:12:55,033
<b>We should try to look at these people in</b>

391
01:12:55,033 --> 01:12:56,466
<b>their historical context</b>

392
01:12:56,533 --> 01:12:57,566
<b>without justifying</b>

393
01:12:57,600 --> 01:12:58,966
<b>everything that they did.</b>

394
01:12:59,633 --> 01:13:01,033
<b>That's what I try to do here.</b>

395
01:13:01,233 --> 01:13:03,133
<b>I go to the sources and tell you the</b>

396
01:13:03,133 --> 01:13:05,033
<b>history, even when it's uncomfortable,</b>

397
01:13:05,366 --> 01:13:07,333
<b>even when it goes against a common story.</b>

398
01:13:08,000 --> 01:13:08,766
<b>If that's the kind of</b>

399
01:13:08,766 --> 01:13:11,566
<b>history you want, please subscribe.</b>

